        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="lzh" xml:space="preserve">
<ab>
<lb n="01"/>摩訶
<lb n="02"/>衍經
<lb n="01"/>
<lb n="T08n0223_0250b02"/><supplied reason="lost">菩 大 薩 摩訶薩 摩訶衍，復次，須菩提</supplied>！<supplied reason="lost">菩</supplied>薩
<lb n="02"/><supplied reason="lost">摩訶薩</supplied>復有<supplied reason="lost">摩訶衍，所謂内空</supplied>、外空、
<lb n="03"/><supplied reason="lost">内外空，空空、大空，</supplied>弟<supplied reason="lost">一義空</supplied>，有
<lb n="04"/><supplied reason="lost">為空</supplied>、<supplied reason="lost">無爲空，畢竟空、無始空，</supplied>散
<lb n="05"/>
<lb n="T08n0223_0250b06"/><unclear>空</unclear>、<supplied reason="lost">性空，自相空、 諸法空</supplied>、<supplied reason="lost">不</supplied><unclear>可</unclear><supplied reason="lost">得</supplied>
<lb n="06"/><supplied reason="lost">空，無法空、有法空、無法有法空。</supplied>
</ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus"/>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                <p>“Mahayana Sutra” The Mahayana of the bodhisattva—furthermore, Subhūti , the Mahayana of the bodhisattva-mahāsattva —[consists of] what is called the emptiness of the internal, the emptiness of the external, the emptiness of what is both internal and external, the emptiness of emptiness, the great emptiness, the emptiness of the supreme truth, the emptiness of the conditioned, the emptiness of the unconditioned, the emptiness of the final, the emptiness of the beginningless, the emptiness of the analyzed, the emptiness of [intrinsic] nature, the emptiness of self attributes, the emptiness of all entities, the emptiness of non-obtainability, the emptiness of non-existent entities, the emptiness of existent entities, [and] the emptiness of entities that are both existent and non-existent.</p>
            </div>
